{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>A donkey or an ox or a sheep.</b> This passage concerns a paid guardian, for the way to guard them is only for pay, because there is toil in guarding them — to take them out and bring them in, to feed them and water them. And when he deposited them on condition to guard them from thieves and wolves, he deposited them with him." "<b>Or died.</b> On its own." "<b>Or was broken.</b> By beasts — as in 'and did not break the donkey.'" "<b>Or was captured.</b> By bandits. All of these are instances of unforeseen compulsion, for if not, it should have said 'and is stolen' as above." "<b>There is no witness.</b> This refers to 'was captured.' Above, in the passage of the unpaid guardian, there was no occasion to write 'there is no witness,' for it is obvious to us that the way of theft is only in secret."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:45.616906297Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}